	(text "36 V SUPPLY BOARD. Brake turns on at 40.2-42.2 V (RV1), off 2 V lower; keep it under the motor\ncontrollers' limit (moteus r4: 44 V). Set RV1 for about 41 V and check at TP4 before connecting motors.\nBRAKE RESISTOR (off-board, J9/J10): Arcol HS100 4R7 J, 4.7 ohm 100 W aluminium-housed.\nBolt it to metal (100 W needs a heatsink). Brake current 8.6-9.0 A at the 40.2-42.2 V trip; use 16 AWG.\nThermal cut-out: NC bimetal (e.g. KSD301 NC 100 C) clamped to it, wired into the E-stop loop -\nnot in series with the brake current (bimetal contacts are not rated to break 9 A DC)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 129.54 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c7cb3a5d-7621-4af5-924f-8b5983ac993e")
	)
